p('What the confidence calculation does','h');p('A path is one trial, with success only if EVERY dated payment is made, within$0.000001roundoff. Assets and payment dates are not extra trials. With zero misses,299independent paths is the minimum for a one-sided95%Clopper-Pearson lower bound reaching99%. The600path coarse final run has lower bound99.502%; the1600path run has99.813%.')
p('That bound assumes independent generated paths conditional on frozen fitted inputs and the validation-selected fixed portfolio. It does not validate the economic law. The validation version is a selection screen, not post-selection coverage. EP-weighted nominal/stressed fractions are descriptive model rates, not binomial confidence bounds. Imported scenario archives are refused in this strict mode because their independence is unverified.','small')
